visible_assistant_text.text:
This confirms it clearly: before commit `ac494c6c2710a207f51a219e3b09360a9c94203c`, both branches correctly placed `+ link` **inside** `wrapInHtml(...)`. That commit refactored the if/else into a ternary expression but moved `+ link` **outside** the parentheses of `wrapInHtml(...)`, producing malformed tooltip HTML (link text appended after the closing `</html>` tag). The fix commit simply re-adds the parentheses to restore the original intended grouping.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: ac494c6c2710a207f51a219e3b09360a9c94203c

## Reasoning
(1) I traced the full history of the modified line/method in `LocalInspectionsPass.java` using `git log -p --follow` on the file, searching for `wrapInHtml` occurrences to find every time this tooltip-construction logic was touched. This revealed the line was rewritten from an if/else form into a ternary form in commit `ac494c6c2710a207f51a219e3b09360a9c94203c` ("more diagnostics for EA-68014"), and that this is the immediate parent version of the line the fix commit touches.

(2) In that commit, the original code was:
```java
if (message.startsWith("<html>")) {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message) + link);
}
else {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message) + link);
}
```
and it was refactored into:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link ;
```
This refactor is not semantically equivalent: in both original branches, `+ link` was inside the `wrapInHtml(...)` call. In the new ternary version, `+ link` ended up **outside** the `wrapInHtml(...)` call due to a missing set of parentheses. This means `link` (an HTML `<a>` tag pointing to the inspection description) gets appended after the closing `</html>` tag rather than inside it, producing malformed/broken HTML tooltip markup.

(3) The bug-fixing commit's diff exactly restores the intended grouping by wrapping the ternary expression plus `link` in parentheses passed to `wrapInHtml`:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml((message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link);
```
This is a one-token (parenthesis placement) fix that directly reverses the regression introduced in `ac494c6c2710a207f51a219e3b09360a9c94203c`. The malformed HTML tooltip is consistent with the reported symptom "Not all warnings are displayed in the editor" (broken tooltip HTML can interfere with highlighting/rendering of the warning). I'm highly confident in this identification since the diff shows a direct undo of the specific structural change made in that commit, and no other commits touched this line in between.

